      "page_title": "Adding/Removing Shards & Vetting a Key",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A new shard starts empty and fills gradually",
            "Expect hours of background migration, not seconds"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Removing A Shard"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`removeShard` starts draining, poll it until done",
            "First `movePrimary` any unsharded DBs it owns",
            "`movePrimary` is a blocking full copy: schedule it",
            "Survivors need room for the data plus migration headroom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Hardware Never Fixes A Key",
          "text": "Adding shards does not retroactively re-split jumbo chunks. A bad key choice stays bad no matter how many machines you buy."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Five Checks In Order",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "List top query patterns by volume and latency need",
            "Cardinality: distinct values past every chunk you will need",
            "Aim for millions of distinct values, not dozens",
            "Frequency: hunt the fat tail before production finds it",
            "Monotonicity: time-derived means hash or compound prefix"
          ]
        },
        {
