        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.orders.aggregate([",
            "  { $group: { _id: \"$customerId\",",
            "      n: { $sum: 1 } } },",
            "  { $sort: { n: -1 } }, { $limit: 10 }])"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Then verify write distribution, not just stored bytes",
            "Simulate inserts and measure per-shard write rate",
            "Byte balance can hide a shard taking every write"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keys That Work",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shape",
            "Key",
            "Why"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Multi-tenant",
              "{tenantId,_id}",
              "tenant-local reads"
            ],
            [
              "Time series",
              "{deviceId,ts}",
              "history contiguous"
            ],
            [
              "Raw logs",
              "{_id: hashed}",
              "pure write spread"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Why Good Keys Work & Zone Pinning",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`_id` suffix splits a whale tenant into many chunks",
            "`deviceId` prefix spreads devices, keeps a device together",
            "Hashed logs accept scatter-gather reads on purpose"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Zones Pin Ranges",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "sh.addShardToZone(\"shard0\", \"EU\")",
            "sh.updateZoneKeyRange(\"db.users\",",
            "  { region: \"EU\", _id: MinKey },",
            "  { region: \"EU\", _id: MaxKey },",
            "  \"EU\")"
          ],
          "note": "range must be a shard key prefix"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Data residency==: EU customers stay on EU-hosted shards",
            "Tiered disks: recent ranges on NVMe, archive on cheap disk",
            "Overlapping zone ranges are **rejected**; gaps float freely"
          ],
          "style": "star"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anti-Keys, Process Errors & Safe Backups",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keys That Burn",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Anti-key",
            "Failure",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{createdAt:1}",
              "max-key chunk",
              "one shard's speed"
            ],
            [
              "{status:1}",
              "low cardinality",
              "jumbo forever"
            ],
            [
              "random UUID",
              "no locality",
              "every read broadcast"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Compound Trade"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prefix controls locality and targeting",
            "Suffix controls splittability inside the prefix",
            "A prefix you never filter on buys you scatter-gather"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Write The Choice Down",
          "text": "Record the key with its assumptions about traffic shape. When the shape changes, that note tells you whether it is time to reshard."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Process Errors",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sharding too early: one replica set carries more than you think",
            "Sharding too late: a full hot cluster has no I/O headroom",
            "Reading chunk counts as if they were bytes per shard",
            "Connecting straight to a shard's `mongod` for reads"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Expecting global unique indexes to exist",
            "Only shard-key-prefixed unique indexes work at all",
            "Leaving the balancer on during a snapshot backup",
            "That snapshot captures an inconsistent chunk map"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Before You Commit",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Supporting index on the key prefix already exists",
            "No array, text or float fields in the key",
            "Hot query filters on the ==prefix==",
            "Free disk and I/O headroom for migrations"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Safe Snapshot Backup",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "sh.stopBalancer()",
            "sh.isBalancerRunning() // false?",
            "// ...take filesystem snapshot",
            "sh.startBalancer()"
          ],
          "note": "wait for in-flight migrations to end"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Diagnosis & Repair: Refine vs Reshard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Symptom To Cause"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "What you see",
            "Root cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "One shard 90% CPU, rest idle",
              "hot chunk, monotonic key"
            ],
            [
              "Jumbo chunks in `sh.status()`",
              "cardinality too low"
            ],
            [
              "Every query touches all shards",
              "key absent from hot path"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Repair Tools"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`refineCollectionShardKey` appends a high-cardinality suffix",
            "Appending `_id` breaks up jumbo chunks; build the index first",
            "`reshardCollection` (5.0+) rewrites under a whole new key",
            "It duplicates the data while running: plan disk headroom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Refine In Place"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.orders.createIndex(",
            "  { custId: 1, _id: 1 })",
            "db.adminCommand({",
            "  refineCollectionShardKey:",
            "    \"app.orders\",",
            "  key: { custId: 1, _id: 1 } })"
          ],
          "note": "suffix only: prefix still routes"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Refine Or Reshard?"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Refine",
            "Reshard"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Version",
              "4.4+",
              "5.0+"
            ],
            [
              "Change prefix",
              "no",
              "**yes**"
            ],
            [
              "Data copy",
              "none",
              "full"
            ],
            [
              "Disk cost",
              "new index",
              "~2× data"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Try Refine First",
          "text": "If the prefix is still right and only chunks are too coarse, refine is cheap. Reshard only when the prefix itself is wrong."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Reshard Prerequisites"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Free disk for a ==full second copy== of the collection",
            "Index for the new key can be built during the run",
            "Low-traffic window for the commit's write pause"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Find Jumbo Chunks"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "use config",
            "db.chunks.find({ jumbo: true })",
            "db.orders.getShardDistribution()"
          ],
          "note": "count chunks, then check real bytes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Resharding, Monitoring & Reading Explain",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.adminCommand({",
            "  reshardCollection: \"app.orders\",",
            "  key: { tenantId: 1, orderId: 1 } })",
            "// online, but commit pauses writes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Resharding Is Not Free",
          "text": "It runs online, yet the commit holds a short critical section. Expect a write pause at the very end of the operation."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Orphan Cleanup"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`cleanupOrphaned` and the range deleter remove strays",
            "4.4+ filters orphans automatically on shard reads",
            "Application logic still enforces non-prefixed uniqueness"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Watch These Five"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Monitoring Set",
          "items": [
            "Per-shard write ops and per-shard data size",
            "Chunk migration counts over time",
            "Balancer round failures",
            "Jumbo chunk count, alert on any increase"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Cluster is slow. First command?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`sh.status()` for keys, jumbo flags, balancer state",
            "`getShardDistribution()` for real bytes per shard",
            "`explain(\"executionStats\").shards` on the hot query"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Whole Chain",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "shard key",
              "chunk",
              "shard",
              "one hop"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cluster = shards + config servers (CSRS) + `mongos`",
            "Only `mongos` holds the whole routing map",
            "Key to chunk to shard is the model; the rest is bookkeeping"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Read The Explain",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.orders.find({ tenantId: 7 })",
            "  .explain(\"executionStats\")",
            "// SINGLE_SHARD = targeted",
            "// SHARD_MERGE = scatter-gather"
          ],
          "note": "count entries in shards[]"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Latency Budget",
          "text": "App → mongos → shard(s) → back adds a network round trip. Budget it in every SLO."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Key Quality, Scatter Signals & Orphans",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Key Quality"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "High cardinality, flat frequency, non-monotonic",
            "And present in the queries you actually run",
            "Miss any one of the four and you pay for it daily"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One entry in `shards[]` means the key did its job",
            "Every shard listed means the ==prefix== is missing",
            "Scatter latency tracks the **slowest** shard, not the average"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Orphans Mislead",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`count()` on a shard can include orphaned documents",
            "Direct `mongod` reads miss data living on other shards",
            "Always read through `mongos`, never around it"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Recap: The Sharding Cheat Sheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ranged Or Hashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Inserts",
            "Range reads"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Ranged",
              "hotspot risk",
              "targeted"
            ],
            [
              "Hashed",
              "even",
              "broadcast"
            ],
            [
              "Compound hashed",
              "even",
              "zone-able prefix"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`{ region: 1, userId: \"hashed\" }` is the middle path",
            "Shard key present = one shard = one hop",
            "Key absent = every shard = slowest-shard latency"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Balancer And Zones"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Chunk default 128 MB in 6.0+; jumbo means unsplittable",
            "Balancer runs on the config primary, sizes data in 6.0+",
            "Confine it with `activeWindow` during peak hours",
            "Migration blocks the moving range only, briefly",
            "Zones win before evenness: residency and tiered disks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Escape Routes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`refineCollectionShardKey`: append a suffix (4.4+)",
            "`reshardCollection`: full rewrite (5.0+)",
            "Neither is cheap, both beat living with a jumbo chunk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "sh.status()",
            "db.coll.getShardDistribution()",
            "db.currentOp({ desc: /Migration/ })",
            "use config; db.chunks.find({ jumbo: true })"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Buy Hardware Last",
          "text": "Adding shards fixes capacity and never fixes a bad key. Get the key right, then scale the machine count."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Final Rule",
          "items": [
            "Pick the key for the query you run a million times a day",
            "Verify it against real data volumes and real skew",
            "Only then commit: the decision is close to permanent"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of MONGODB SHARDING. Your shard key is the one decision MongoDB will not let you take back cheaply, and most teams pick it from the field that felt like the natural primary key. This handbook walks the full chain: cluster anatomy, how keys turn documents into chunks, ranged vs hashed, why a missing key turns every read into a scatter-gather, and what the balancer is actually doing while your p99 spikes. Ends with the decision framework and the repair commands you hope you never need.",
